// CPU per target and bin, after Live.CpuTimeline.kql and Dashboard.SelectTargets.kql: for T1 and T2 the SQL Server
// process's share of all logical CPUs on the machine (SQLProcessCPUPercent), for T3 a percentage of the service tier's
// limit (AvgCPUPercent); Live.CpuTimeline.kql says why
// (https://learn.microsoft.com/fabric/database/hub/microsoft-sql-query-performance-monitoring-telemetry, checked
// 2026-10-26). The highest instance average in each bin.
| summarize CpuPercent = round(max(AvgCPU), 1) by Target, Bucket
| order by Bucket asc
